═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STATEMENT OF ORIGINALITY (CODE ONLY)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The following elements of this repository are original works authored
by Hazem Soussi (HA):

  ✓ All Python, JavaScript, HTML, and CSS source code
  ✓ Procedural sprite-drawing routines (Mario, hearts, tiles, particles)
  ✓ Procedural audio (Web Audio API tones, no sampled assets)
  ✓ The level layout string in `mario_gta6_2d.py` and its parser
  ✓ The two-currency (coins + credits) reward system
  ✓ The game-loop, physics integrator, and HUD composition
  ✓ The website design, build system, and module organization
  ✓ The documentation, audit report, and contributor workflow

The following elements are DERIVATIVE — they recreate gameplay patterns
that are part of the public vocabulary of the platformer genre and
specifically reference the works listed in TRADEMARKS.md. They are
included under fair use for educational, non-commercial fan purposes,
and would be reworked or removed under any future licensing agreement
with the relevant IP holders:

  • The protagonist's cap-and-overalls silhouette and red/blue palette
  • The mushroom, fire-flower, and star power-up progression
  • Question-mark blocks, breakable brick blocks, and pipe geometry
  • The koopa-troopa and goomba enemy archetypes and their stomping
    resolution
  • The "1-1" style horizontal-scrolling level structure
  • The coin pickup SFX (E5→G5 square-wave arpeggio)

This distinction is intentional and is offered in good faith so that
any future partnership discussion has a clear picture of what is
original code versus what is respectfully-inspired homage.
